Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns in the GSOD day‑summary tables  

• `stn`: station identifier – filter for LaGuardia (725030).  
• `year`: 4‑digit year – pick every year 2011‑2020.  
• `mo`: month – filter for ‘06’ (June).  
• `da`: day – filter for ‘12’.  
• `temp`: mean daily temperature (°F) – take as the average temperature.  
• `wdsp`: mean daily wind speed (knots, stored as STRING) – CAST to FLOAT64, then average.  
• `prcp`: total daily precipitation (inches) – use as precipitation amount.  

Optional lookup table  

• `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` (`usaf`, `wban`, `name`, …) – join on  
  `stn = usaf` to confirm that station **725030** is “NEW YORK LGA, NY US”.

Conditions you will generally use  

`WHERE stn = '725030'  
  AND mo = '06'  
  AND da = '12'  
  AND year BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'`  

(when using a wildcard table you instead restrict `_TABLE_SUFFIX` between '2011' and '2020').


Below are ten progressively richer example queries (each limited to 20 rows) that one could run to explore the data and finally obtain the requested result.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at LaGuardia records in 2011
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`
WHERE stn = '725030'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. See which June days have data for LaGuardia in 2011
SELECT DISTINCT da
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`
WHERE stn = '725030' AND mo = '06'
ORDER BY da
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect the single record for 12 Jun 2011
SELECT year, mo, da, temp, wdsp, prcp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`
WHERE stn = '725030' AND mo = '06' AND da = '12'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Join with the stations table to double‑check the station name
SELECT g.year, g.mo, g.da, s.name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011` AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
  ON g.stn = s.usaf AND g.wban = s.wban
WHERE g.stn = '725030' AND g.mo = '06' AND g.da = '12'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Pull 12 Jun rows for LaGuardia from every year 2011‑2020
SELECT year, temp, wdsp, prcp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`
WHERE stn = '725030' AND mo = '06' AND da = '12'
UNION ALL
SELECT year, temp, wdsp, prcp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2012`
WHERE stn = '725030' AND mo = '06' AND da = '12'
-- …repeat through 2020…
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same as #5 but add CAST for wind speed and compute simple averages
SELECT year,
       AVG(temp)  AS avg_temp_f,
       AVG(CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64)) AS avg_wind_knots,
       AVG(prcp)  AS avg_prcp_in
FROM (
  SELECT year, temp, wdsp, prcp FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`  WHERE stn='725030' AND mo='06' AND da='12'
  UNION ALL
  SELECT year, temp, wdsp, prcp FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2012`  WHERE stn='725030' AND mo='06' AND da='12'
  -- …repeat through 2020…
)
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Examine NULL / missing value patterns on 12 Jun for all years
SELECT year,
       temp,
       SAFE_CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64) AS wdsp_knots,
       prcp,
       CASE WHEN temp = 9999.9 THEN 'temp_missing' END AS temp_flag,
       CASE WHEN prcp = 99.99  THEN 'prcp_missing' END AS prcp_flag
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
  AND stn = '725030' AND mo = '06' AND da = '12'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Use the wildcard table to pull just the three columns of interest
SELECT _TABLE_SUFFIX AS yr,
       temp AS temp_f,
       CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64) AS wind_knots,
       prcp AS prcp_in
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
  AND stn = '725030' AND mo = '06' AND da = '12'
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Compute the average (they are single‑row per day, but keeping AVG for completeness)
SELECT _TABLE_SUFFIX AS year,
       AVG(temp)                          AS avg_temp_f,
       AVG(SAFE_CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64))    AS avg_wind_knots,
       AVG(prcp)                          AS prcp_in
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
  AND stn = '725030' AND mo = '06' AND da = '12'
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer query: average temperature, mean wind speed, and precipitation
--     for LaGuardia (station 725030) on 12 June, 2011‑2020
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX                       AS year,
  ROUND(AVG(temp),                    1) AS avg_temp_f,
  ROUND(AVG(CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64)),   1) AS avg_wind_knots,
  ROUND(AVG(prcp),                    2) AS prcp_in
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
  AND stn = '725030'
  AND mo  = '06'
  AND da  = '12'
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year;
```

